\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'a0In a near distant future, the world lives in a dystopia characterised by underwater cities due to a nuclear war. Humanity is taught one rule from birth, the surface\'92s air is toxic. According to the government, the air still has radioactivity within it, even after thousands of years of living underwater, and anyone exposed to it without the proper equipment will die in seconds.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 Those in power take advantage of this belief in order to control society to benefit themselves. The only people allowed on the surface are people known as the divers, an elite group of highly trained explorers equipped with specialised equipment, these people are treated like heroes due to their bravery and the courage they have to go up to the surface and face the toxic air.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 Schools teach stories about how poisonous the air is, and tell children about the worst deaths that people suffered after going to the surface. Every underwater city is sealed by one big dome, protecting people from the outside air.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs45\fsmilli22667 \cf0 \strokec2 Possible Ending 1 \'97 The Hopeful Ending
\f1\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Mira broadcasts undeniable proof to every underwater city at once. Citizens panic at first, but gradually people begin traveling to the surface. Humanity experiences sunlight, wind, and open skies for the first time in centuries. The underwater cities become symbols of survival rather than prisons, and society slowly rebuilds a free civilization above the ocean.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs45\fsmilli22667 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Possible Ending 2 \'97 The Dark Ending
\f1\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Before Mira can reveal the truth, Chancellor Veyr declares martial law. Kael is captured, and the government destroys all evidence of the breathable surface. Mira escapes alone to the surface, where she survives in secret while billions remain trapped underwater, still believing the air is poison. The story ends with her staring at the ocean below, realizing humanity may never learn the truth.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs45\fsmilli22667 \cf0 Possible Ending 3 \'97 The Bittersweet Ending
\f1\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Mira exposes the lie, but the revelation throws society into chaos. Riots erupt across the underwater cities, systems fail, and thousands die during the collapse of government control. In the end, survivors reach the surface and begin again, but humanity is deeply divided \'97 some grateful for freedom, others believing the lie kept civilization alive. The story closes with Mira wondering whether the truth always leads to a better world.
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

